  "underlying": "004acea2e23056bc79415cfa69b9f3ea4254e6d0 Paid fast-lane order 9494e9ea (public). Qwen3.5-4B fine-tune served by the author's own torchcast_decision package, measured as shipped: the author's server unchanged at tag v1.3.0 with its bundled decision_config.json (repository torchcast-ai/torchcast-decision-4b at the pinned commit above). Same runtime as the v1.2 row: official pytorch/pytorch:2.9.1-cuda12.8-cudnn9-devel image (digest-pinned) plus an offline hash-locked overlay of the documented packages (transformers 5.8.1, flash-linear-attention 0.5.2, causal-conv1d 1.7.0), on Python 3.11 instead of the documented 3.12. decision_config.json sets attention_mode noncausal_full_attention (the full-attention layers see the whole prompt in both directions, as trained; causal runtimes such as vLLM give different probabilities) and a disclosed yes/no commit floor of 0.801: a yes/no probability with max(P, 1-P) below 0.801 is moved to 0.801 on its own side (answer unchanged; same mechanism as h2o-lightning-4b, v1.1 and v1.2). New in v1.3: new fine-tuned weights; calibration temperature 0.9 (v1.2 used 1.0); CUDA graphs in the non-causal mode (speed only: graph and eager readouts were bit-identical in our check). Prompts over 16,384 tokens keep the head and the tail of the state (documented). Output tokens are 0 (no generation). All 1,500 items answered, none refused; the 15 states longer than 16,384 tokens are cut by the model to head and tail and scored as answered, as for earlier truncated rows. No decision took more than 10 seconds (maximum 7.73 s). The cost is a labelled estimate on the Qwen3.5-4B base-model reference, not a price the author or a host charges. Self-hosted speed adjustment as for every self-hosted row; the device class (A100 SXM4 80GB) is the same as for v1.2. v1.3 is a new row next to v1.2; v1.2 remains listed as its own version.",
